# connector inline client re-parses the CA bundle PEM on every request (B314 port not memoized)

## Steps to Reproduce

1. TODO: Add steps

## Expected Behavior

TODO: Describe expected behavior

## Actual Behavior

TODO: Describe actual behavior

## Symptom

Found during B325 (2026-09-18, C5 group): the ticket text claimed the connector-side CA bundle parse was covered, but only ocaml/relay_client.ml was memoized (per-bundle-path TLS ctx with mtime invalidation). The connector's INLINE client port (B314, net_ctx_of_bundle at ocaml/c2c_relay_connector.ml ~2279) still re-parses the PEM and builds the conduit/TLS context on EVERY request while C2C_RELAY_CA_BUNDLE is set.

## Impact

Per-request parse cost on the machine connector loop (every heartbeat/register/send/poll of every root, every pass) against hosts using a private/self-signed HTTPS relay with a CA bundle. Wasteful but not a correctness bug.

## Fix direction

Port the B325 memoization (module-level table keyed by bundle path, invalidate on mtime change, never cache failed parses) to the connector inline client.

## Evidence

Verified in the B325 group report (C5); deliberately out of that ticket's scope (it pinned relay_client behavior only).